<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0222afe66338> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Rest assured that no matter how sophisticated the current facial swapping technology is, it can not deceive our payment apps." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9568" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/077533520f9c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Creating convincing fake audio and video — known as “deepfakes” — isn’t new, but it previously took a great deal of time, skill and money." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9568" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/121a0177169a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Protesters in Hong Kong are going to great lengths to cover their faces over fears that police are using facial recognition technology to identify and arrest targets." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9566" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/17388b561ea4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On Tuesday, Zao said it had changed its user agreement to address “concerns about privacy and safety issues.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9568" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/195ef5b8e03d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[9564] A newly released face-swapping app has come under fire for a clause in its terms and conditions allowing it to sell users’ photos and videos." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/27085d792535> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Concerns about fraudulent use of the app even prompted a response from Alipay, a popular Chinese online payment system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9568" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/27e0f1fe5176> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After downloading the app, users are asked to upload photos of themselves that can be used to make a face-flipped clip of their choice." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2831d29f76e5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The issues raised by Zao are reminiscent of FaceApp, another viral app that uses AI to transform user photos." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9568" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/28de2a99ecfc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The episode replayed a similar controversy over FaceApp, a photo-editing app that went viral in July." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9569" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/40f7fbbe9ca2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ZAO致歉：称不会存个人面部生物识别特征信息，无支付风险" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9563" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/44bef5eaf31b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Chinese ‘Deepfake’ App Censured Over Privacy Concerns" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4f7931e731a9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Zao users have been sharing self-made videos on their social feeds on WeChat, Tencent’s ubiquitous messaging app." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/61bba652e4ed> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ZAO的运营团队，还对此前给大家造成疑虑和困扰再次致歉。" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9563" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6b90e7e0ab35> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Zao, a free deepfake face-swapping app that’s able to place your likeness into scenes from hundreds of movies and TV shows after uploading just a single photograph, has gone viral in China." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9566" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6e2966b887bc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On Tuesday, Zao said it had changed its user agreement to address “concerns about privacy and safety issues.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9568" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/815c61138e60> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ZAO, a viral Chinese app that uses AI to face-swap users and famous actors, is now embroiled in a major privacy controversy." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9569" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/86fbbd4663a2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Zao — meaning “make,” “build,” or “fabricate” in Mandarin — turns users into “stars” by digitally grafting their faces onto the bodies of celebrities in scenes from movies, TV shows, and music videos to create what is known as a “deepfake,” a technological portmanteau combining “deep learning” and “fake.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8b48be199384> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Meanwhile, on China’s other dominant social app, microblogging platform Weibo, a hashtag about Zao content being partially blocked on WeChat had been viewed over 160 million times by Monday evening." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9d0bf51eb84f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Zao said in its Tuesday statement that the use of its system would not cause “payment risks,” adding that the “security threshold for facial recognition payment is extremely high.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9568" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a1c4721f95ae> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It’s the latest—and perhaps most impressive—application of generative adversarial networks, or GANs, the AI algorithms behind deepfakes." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9569" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a5887c3ca355> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[9569] ZAO, a viral Chinese app that uses AI to face-swap users and famous actors, is now embroiled in a major privacy controversy." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9569" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b07957cfe6c7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A newly released face-swapping app has come under fire for a clause in its terms and conditions allowing it to sell users’ photos and videos." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b5736ee450ce> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Another convincing deepfake app goes viral prompting immediate privacy backlash" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9566" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b8d224160db3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[9568] On Tuesday, Zao said it had changed its user agreement to address “concerns about privacy and safety issues.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9568" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c9f72a23b171> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "An AI app that turns you into a movie star has risked the privacy of millions" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9569" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ca2aa139d5ba> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The app, called Zao, works by superimposing an image of the user’s face onto a character in a video or GIF using artificial intelligence (AI)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9568" .

