<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8194bcac1c3b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A newly released face-swapping app has come under fire for a clause in its terms and conditions allowing it to sell users’ photos and videos." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9dda7239101f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A newly released face-swapping app has come under fire for a clause in its terms and conditions allowing it to sell users’ photos and videos." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b74d94dc9666> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ZAO, a viral Chinese app that uses AI to face-swap users and famous actors, is now embroiled in a major privacy controversy." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9569" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d8ea53186380> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "WeChat, China’s top social-networking app, also banned any sharing of footage or photos from ZAO." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9569" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3e4db03d6cd5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In February, a deepfake video of mainland actor Yang Mi’s face convincingly superimposed onto Hong Kong actor Athena Chu’s body went viral on Weibo, prompting its creator to come forward and explain that he had merely wanted to make people “more aware of how (deepfakes) could be used in the future.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2039ac28fd9d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "WeChat, China’s top social-networking app, also banned any sharing of footage or photos from ZAO." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9569" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/351e96598317> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Since its release Friday, Zao has rocketed up the charts to become the No. 2 most widely downloaded free app on Apple’s China app store as of Monday evening." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3bec52816873> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "9月1日，澎湃新闻记者注意到，打出“仅需一张照片，出演天下好戏”口号的“ZAO”，微信分享链接已停止访问。" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9563" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cb26359fab76> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On Monday, a Chengdu-based lawyer who blogs under the pen name Fashanshu explained that, under Article 41 of China’s cybersecurity law, network operators are forbidden from sharing citizens’ personal information." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f46dccdcf82c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "1 Twitter user, Allan Xia, uploaded a video of his face swapped with Leonardo DiCaprio’s." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9568" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9acce7c6c36a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Zao, a free deepfake face-swapping app that’s able to place your likeness into scenes from hundreds of movies and TV shows after uploading just a single photograph, has gone viral in China." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9566" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d5e3680f01ec> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lei Xiaoliang — head of the Changsha-based company that developed Zao — also co-founded Momo, one of China’s most popular dating apps." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/AISystem/837b0a7770e3> a airo:AISystem ;
    rdfs:label "FaceApp" ;
    airo:confidenceScore "0.99"^^xsd:float ;
    airo:extractionMode "explicit" ;
